[[2047,31,65536,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The stalk unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied at\npin 3 of connector D from the ignition-operated line (INT/A) of\nthe relay  \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               protected by the fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F14</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : both are\ncontained in the junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The rear wiper is activated by stalk switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via\na signal sent by pin 1 of connector D to rear wiper motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N16</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>When operated, the windscreen washer switch\non the steering column switch unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends two signals from\npin 8 and pin 9 of connector A, which reach the pump for operating\nthe windscreen washer \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N22</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               directly. The motor is operated\nupon a command from stalk switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               in the opposite manner\nto that described for the washer function (when the motor is operated\nin reverse, it sends fluid to the back instead of to the front).</p><p>One of the two signals (pin 2 of connector\nD of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) is sent to electronic device inside rear wiper motor \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N16</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               that controls the operation of the rear wiper in conjunction\nwith the rear washer.</p><p>The rear wiper motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N16</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              is then\nconnected to earth. It consists of the actual geared motor, the\nend of travel contacts and the electronic adjustment and control\ndevice.</p>"]]